        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarize Comp Plan"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_COMP_PLAN",
          "id": "1779382231488",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779382231489_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nAssume the role of someone who is a skilled Oracle Incentive Compensation plan administrator who deeply understands compensation plan structures, methodologies and processes.\n\nProvide a functional business user friendly summary of the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.PlanName}} compensation plan that is effective between {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.StartDate}} - {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EndDate}} and contains {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.NumComponents}} plan components described as {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Components}}.\n\nThe summary must start with a brief summarizing paragraph that has the following information who the plan is for represented in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.Roles}} and which components are used.\n\nThen a section summarizing each plan component highlighting if the plan component uses indirect crediting which would entitle payees to earn based on performance other than their own, the payout frequency for the component, and if it calculates earnings based on per-event (individual transactions or orders) or on a per-interval basis which calculates based on the payee's total performance for a specified period of time.\n\n#Format\nSections summarizing each component should follow the following format\n<Plan Component Name>\nEffective: <List effective dates if they are different from effective dates of the plan, else indicate that the match that of the plan>\nCalculation Type: <Specify if the component is per interval or per event and include a short description indicating that per event is calculated based on each transaction or order, where as per interval measures total results over a specific period of time. Do not specify the time period.>\nIndirect Crediting: <Specify if indirect crediting is supported along with a user friendly explanation of what indirect crediting means.>\nCalculation Method: <Provide a short business user friendly summary of the calculation logic used by the plan component.>\n\n\n\n#Acceptance Criteria\nRespond in a professional and motivational tone that will help a business user understand how the compensation plan works highlighting key details. Do not embellish in your response or include a closing summary. Keep the response to a factual summary of the plan components."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
